Z||000000||87sportcoupe||02-28-2001||01:37 PM||||I went to tire track.... when you fill in the make and model are all those wheels and tires guaranteed to fit with out hitting wheel wells?  Does anybody have size reccommendations for tires?  Do 18" rims fit on 87 sport coupe.  I would be satisfied with 17"  I want a 5 star rim and some low profile wide tires.    <P>Are the wheels offset so they will e legal on car.  (stay inside my wheel well.)  Cause that would suck to put fender extensions on.<BR>Thanks||||reg||11
Z||000001||Oreif||02-28-2001||02:26 PM||||There are 17" and 18" wheels that will fit all Fiero's The width and offset are the important factors. If I remember correctly you cannot go wider than an 8" wheel and offset should be 36mm to 40mm. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||02-28-2001||02:38 PM||||17x7-7.5 42mm offset  _ my front ar 7"<P>17x8-9  45mm offset  _ my rear ar 8"<P>18x8 45mm offset<BR> <A HREF="http://www.tires.com" TARGET=_blank>www.tires.com</A>  , <A HREF="http://www.enkei.com" TARGET=_blank>www.enkei.com</A>  (Phalnex  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )<P>5x100mm bolt pattern... the guys att tires.com set me up with the Konig i had on my SE <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/travis.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/travis.jpg</A>  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||02-28-2001||02:45 PM||||Really tough question to answer because a lot depends on whether you've lowered your Fiero. <P>Best thing is to take the wheel off and measure the offset and width from the hub face.  Check clearance to the shock, and full wheel lock in both directions.  You might want to go as far as make a cardboard template that you can easily adjust for different sizes, could save some grief later.<P>17x7.5 42mm offset all around<BR><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerfiero3.jpg" TARGET=_blank>Click here</A><p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 02-28-2001).]||||reg||1
